1
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:07,160
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

2
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,840
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:16,160
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,440
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

5
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,200
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,360
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

7
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,800
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

8
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,800
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

9
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:30,680
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,360
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

11
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,840
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

12
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:40,640
♪Come, share a cup with me♪

13
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,600
(Welcome to Cold Palace Refreshments)

14
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,480
=Farm Busily in the Cold Palace=

15
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,680
(Based on Hongshu.com's novel
I'm Busy Farming in the Cold Palace)

16
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:49,680
=Episode 4=

17
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:52,880
Who let you in?

18
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,759
Who are you?

19
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:58,039
Speak of a handsome man,

20
00:00:58,039 --> 00:00:59,399
and here he comes!

21
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,479
Heh-heh.

22
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:02,320
My lady, you know him?

23
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:06,400
He's Prince Chen.

24
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,920
The one who gave me that pendant.

25
00:01:08,159 --> 00:01:09,120
Heh-heh.

26
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,239
Oh, wow.

27
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:17,879
Eight-pack abs in the flesh!

28
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:19,200
Come look!

29
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,959
Way better than seeing it in a drama.

30
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:23,680
Hmph.

31
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:26,640
A full stomach really does
bring out the dirty thoughts.

32
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:29,159
You seem to be enjoying life
in the Cold Palace, Empress.

33
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,519
How do you know I'm the Empress?

34
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:36,760
Do I know too much,

35
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,760
or not enough?

36
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:41,439
Too much? Too little?

37
00:01:41,439 --> 00:01:43,040
What are you talking about?

38
00:01:43,519 --> 00:01:44,280
Yinshuang.

39
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,519
Take me back to bed.

40
00:01:45,519 --> 00:01:46,239
Yes, my lady.

41
00:02:01,879 --> 00:02:02,519
You mustn't!

42
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:03,359
Prince Chen!

43
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:04,879
You're His Majesty's uncle!

44
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,879
What if someone sees you?

45
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:07,719
Hmph.

46
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:09,960
Shout a little louder.

47
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,240
Let everyone hear.

48
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,560
Then you can all die together.

49
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,439
I'd sooner give my life

50
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,080
than let my lady come to harm.

51
00:02:20,479 --> 00:02:21,680
A loyal maid indeed.

52
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,400
A loyal maid indeed.

53
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:25,000
Pity you serve the wrong lady.

54
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,759
Pity you serve the wrong lady.

55
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:34,319
A face that handsome?

56
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:35,520
It'd be a shame not to sleep with you.

57
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,560
I'm keeping you all night!

58
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,800
My lady!

59
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,479
First a maid,

60
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:50,879
then a eunuch.

61
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,479
I was going to let you off.

62
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,439
Yet you made a fool of me.

63
00:02:54,759 --> 00:02:55,520
Let go!

64
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,840
You're hurting me!

65
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,000
If you insist on fleeing these walls,

66
00:02:59,719 --> 00:03:01,360
I'll have to clip your wings.

67
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,400
Finished already?

68
00:03:43,719 --> 00:03:45,599
Like lady, like maid.

69
00:03:46,039 --> 00:03:48,599
Why are your clothes undone,
Your Highness?

70
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,039
Your lady threw up.

71
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:52,599
Go in and tend to her.

72
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,719
Threw up?

73
00:03:55,599 --> 00:03:57,120
(My lady, are you all right?)

74
00:03:58,639 --> 00:03:59,639
(Don't go!)

75
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,199
(Prince Chen, where are you?)

76
00:04:02,479 --> 00:04:04,159
(My lady, please stop talking.)

77
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:05,680
(Prince Chen, don't go!)

78
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,159
(I booked you for the whole night!)

79
00:04:15,439 --> 00:04:16,199
My lady.

80
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:18,160
Have this hangover remedy before bed.

81
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,360
This room was empty last time.

82
00:04:37,639 --> 00:04:39,399
The private realm can be upgraded too?

83
00:04:39,639 --> 00:04:41,279
(Correct. Congratulations.)

84
00:04:41,439 --> 00:04:44,120
(Virtual Farm upgraded to Level 2.)

85
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:44,480
Wow.

86
00:04:45,079 --> 00:04:46,279
You're pretty clever.

87
00:04:47,399 --> 00:04:49,160
If I keep upgrading,

88
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,279
can this become a mansion?

89
00:04:51,079 --> 00:04:52,360
(In theory, yes.)

90
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,920
(But please note)

91
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,600
(that every upgrade has side effects.)

92
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:57,879
Side effects?

93
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,240
What side effects?

94
00:04:59,959 --> 00:05:01,199
(Currently unknown.)

95
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:03,279
(You must discover them yourself.)

96
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,319
How mysterious.

97
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,519
(To help you grow your crops,)

98
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,199
(your farmland will expand
from 0.67 to 1.33 hectares.)

99
00:05:11,399 --> 00:05:13,839
(Crop growth will be much faster.)

100
00:05:13,839 --> 00:05:16,800
(Smart devices now provide
weather forecasts.)

101
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:18,839
Wow.

102
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,639
I can see the weather outside!

103
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,399
Switch to Donglan.

104
00:05:25,399 --> 00:05:27,079
(Donglan Weather Alert.)

105
00:05:27,399 --> 00:05:28,959
(Tomorrow, 11:45 a.m.)

106
00:05:29,199 --> 00:05:30,800
(Heavy rain for three days.)

107
00:05:32,319 --> 00:05:33,480
With this thing,

108
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,319
those old fogeys at
the Imperial Observatory

109
00:05:35,319 --> 00:05:36,439
will all be out of work.

110
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,560
The drought has lasted for months.

111
00:05:42,839 --> 00:05:45,680
Several northwestern prefectures
have had no harvest at all.

112
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,920
Without rain, unrest is inevitable.

113
00:05:50,399 --> 00:05:51,399
Last night,

114
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:54,439
those old fogeys at the Imperial
Observatory requested an audience.

115
00:05:54,839 --> 00:05:57,120
They want me to pray for rain
at Huguo Temple.

116
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:00,079
Praying would be one thing.

117
00:06:00,439 --> 00:06:03,240
But they insist I set up an altar

118
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:05,439
and make a public
show of praying for rain.

119
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:09,920
They worry for the realm

120
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,680
and wish to reassure the people.

121
00:06:14,959 --> 00:06:17,279
They want me to take the fall

122
00:06:17,959 --> 00:06:20,920
so they can show how much weight
their advice carries.

123
00:06:21,519 --> 00:06:24,279
I'd rather open the state granaries

124
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,399
and give out more relief grain.

125
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,040
Why make a spectacle

126
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,560
and disappoint the people again?

127
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,720
But if your prayers bring rain,

128
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:37,680
then Heaven itself will have affirmed
your mandate.

129
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:41,399
Your grace will bless the realm.

130
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,920
Your name will live on for ages.

131
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,000
(Cold Palace)

132
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,839
My lady.

133
00:06:51,839 --> 00:06:53,160
You really don't remember?

134
00:06:53,839 --> 00:06:54,759
(Last night?)

135
00:06:55,079 --> 00:06:56,319
(What happened last night?)

136
00:06:56,399 --> 00:06:57,959
(Why can't I remember a thing?)

137
00:06:57,959 --> 00:07:00,759
Do you remember Prince Chen?

138
00:07:02,399 --> 00:07:03,360
What Prince Chen?

139
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,839
He came to see you last night.

140
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:07,800
You clung to him

141
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,680
and kept shouting that
you wanted him all night.

142
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,480
No way.

143
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,759
Absolutely not.

144
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,160
Did I get him?

145
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,399
You...

146
00:07:17,519 --> 00:07:18,879
threw up on him.

147
00:07:21,279 --> 00:07:22,759
Could you stop dragging it out?

148
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,240
Come on, Yinshuang.

149
00:07:31,439 --> 00:07:32,639
Let's head to the
hill behind the palace.

150
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,879
It's going to rain for days
starting tomorrow.

151
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,959
Let's pick all the ripe crops.

152
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:43,600
We can't let it all
get ruined in the rain.

153
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,199
Yes, my lady.

154
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,319
(Lu Yunluo.)

155
00:07:45,959 --> 00:07:47,839
(How many secrets are you hiding?)

156
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:52,639
(I heard something curious yesterday.)

157
00:07:52,879 --> 00:07:54,720
(The Empress in the Cold Palace)

158
00:07:54,959 --> 00:07:58,399
(has produced
drought-resistant grain seeds.)

159
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:00,959
My lady.

160
00:08:01,079 --> 00:08:02,480
The sun is scorching.

161
00:08:02,759 --> 00:08:04,160
Will it really rain tomorrow?

162
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,199
If I say it will, it will.

163
00:08:07,279 --> 00:08:08,920
I studied the stars last night.

164
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,759
It'll rain tomorrow at 11:45 a.m.

165
00:08:12,279 --> 00:08:13,199
My lady.

166
00:08:13,199 --> 00:08:15,319
Weren't you asleep last night?

167
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,120
Are you doubting me?

168
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:19,639
No, no, no.

169
00:08:19,639 --> 00:08:20,439
I wouldn't dare.

170
00:08:20,439 --> 00:08:22,199
I believe everything you say.

171
00:08:23,079 --> 00:08:23,879
Let's go.

172
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:26,079
The Imperial Observatory is holding
a rain-prayer ceremony tomorrow.

173
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:26,839
Really?

174
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:27,959
Let's go and watch.

175
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,519
(The drought has ruined every harvest.)

176
00:08:31,879 --> 00:08:33,440
(Yet she managed to grow crops.)

177
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:36,399
(She brews wine, knows farming,)

178
00:08:36,879 --> 00:08:38,639
(and can even read the stars.)

179
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:42,320
(Could it really rain tomorrow?)

180
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,320
His Majesty actually agreed?

181
00:08:57,759 --> 00:08:59,240
How could he refuse

182
00:08:59,639 --> 00:09:01,200
to pray for his people?

183
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:02,440
Master.

184
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,200
You watched the stars for hours.

185
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,960
Will it really rain today?

186
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,600
(Zhao Yuan, Director of the
Imperial Observatory) Never.

187
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:09,759
Won't that invite criticism?

188
00:09:10,159 --> 00:09:11,879
He is the sovereign.

189
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,600
He owes his people an answer.

190
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:19,000
Heaven has appointed me

191
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:20,960
to rule this land.

192
00:09:21,399 --> 00:09:23,360
Yet my people suffer drought.

193
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,000
The land lies barren.

194
00:09:25,639 --> 00:09:26,759
The fault is mine.

195
00:09:32,799 --> 00:09:34,000
My lady.

196
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,440
You're confined to the Cold Palace.

197
00:09:35,879 --> 00:09:37,320
We're doomed if you're caught!

198
00:09:38,279 --> 00:09:39,120
What's there to fear?

199
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,759
It's hardly my first escape.

200
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,440
With a crowd like this,

201
00:09:42,799 --> 00:09:44,080
I can't miss the fun.

202
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,720
I shall bear the blame

203
00:09:58,279 --> 00:09:59,519
and accept heaven's punishment.

204
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,440
I beg heaven for mercy.

205
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,159
Spare my people.

206
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,240
Bless them

207
00:10:05,799 --> 00:10:07,000
with life-giving rain.

208
00:10:09,039 --> 00:10:10,399
We beg heaven for mercy.

209
00:10:10,799 --> 00:10:11,960
Spare the people.

210
00:10:12,559 --> 00:10:13,720
Bless them

211
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,399
with life-giving rain.

212
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:16,600
What time is it?

213
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,159
Just past eleven.

214
00:10:19,919 --> 00:10:21,840
Eleven forty-five.

215
00:10:22,519 --> 00:10:23,679
Here it comes.

216
00:10:31,679 --> 00:10:32,600
The wind's picking up!

217
00:10:44,759 --> 00:10:45,679
Thunder!

218
00:10:52,879 --> 00:10:54,919
It's raining!

219
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,360
Rain! It's really raining!

220
00:10:58,559 --> 00:10:59,879
It really is!

221
00:11:02,279 --> 00:11:03,039
It's raining!

222
00:11:03,039 --> 00:11:03,759
My lady!

223
00:11:04,399 --> 00:11:06,000
After years of drought,

224
00:11:06,399 --> 00:11:10,080
His Majesty's sincerity
has moved Heaven!

225
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:17,120
Long live the Emperor!

226
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:34,120
Eleven forty-five.

227
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,720
You really were telling the truth.

228
00:11:41,759 --> 00:11:43,279
He's the Emperor?

229
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:09,200
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

230
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:13,880
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

231
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:18,200
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

232
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:22,640
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

233
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:26,840
♪Cool dew, starry nights,
wheat sprouts in my hands♪

234
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:31,240
♪I shape fields, not painted brows,
and fill them with hope♪

235
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:35,040
♪Gold and silver bloom from the soil♪

236
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:40,200
♪I smile as the world storms on♪

237
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,000
♪No finery to rival spring♪

238
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:48,480
♪All I wish for are waves of green♪

239
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,600
♪Where is beauty found?♪

240
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:57,320
♪Just lift your eyes and see♪

241
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,360
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

242
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,520
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

243
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,960
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

244
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,960
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

245
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,840
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

246
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,520
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

247
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

248
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:17,360
♪Come, share a cup with me♪
